2.2 Syntax, Keywords, Variables & Comments

```python
"""
This script demonstrates variables, comments, formatted strings,
and dynamic typing using social media and food-order examples.
"""

# Number of Instagram followers
instaFollowers = 1250

# Number of likes on a post
postLikes = 245

# User's name
userName = "Hasnain"

print("Instagram followers:", instaFollowers)
print("Post likes:", postLikes)
print("User name:", userName)

# Favorite food delivery app
foodApp = "Zomato"

# Amount paid for the last order
lastOrderAmount = 450.75

# Whether a coupon was used
usedCoupon = True

# Print the order details using a formatted string
print(
    f"My favorite food delivery app is {foodApp}. "
    f"My last order cost ₹{lastOrderAmount:.2f}. "
    f"Coupon used: {usedCoupon}."
)

# Assign an integer to playlistCount and print it
playlistCount = 12
print(playlistCount)

# Reassign it as a string and print it to demonstrate dynamic typing
playlistCount = "Twelve playlists"
print(playlistCount)
```

